# KiCad-IOS port patch 0049 (KiCad 10.0.1, GPL v3+)
# Round 20, app-wide hunt fixes. The round-20 systematic hunt
# (three censuses: every dialog's modal path, every persisted
# layout key, and a sweep of the rounds 1-19 failure families)
# found more instances of the families this round already
# fixes, plus two small honest-behaviour fixes. All changes
# here are in those families:
#  (1) Fields-table sashes (hunt L4): DIALOG_SYMBOL_FIELDS_TABLE
#      and DIALOG_LIB_FIELDS_TABLE restore their persisted
#      sashes from a ctor-queued CallAfter that runs AFTER
#      DIALOG_SHIM::Show()'s final sash validation -- the
#      verbatim value had the last word, defeating patches
#      0044/0045/0047 for these dialogs. The restores now
#      signature-check the value against the splitter's live
#      extent first (> 60% or < 10% -> 45%).
#      Literal: "round20-fields-sash-guard".
#  (2) Modal KIWAY_PLAYER frames (hunt A3/C-1): ShowModal()
#      disables its top-level parent but never detached, so a
#      chooser frame parented to a dialog (footprint chooser
#      from the symbol properties field grid) is a Qt child of
#      the disabled dialog and opens grey-dead -- the round-19
#      failure one level up. ShowModal() now calls
#      KIPLATFORM::UI::ReparentModal() after Show/Raise/SetFocus
#      and before the disabler, mirroring patch 0046's dialog
#      fix. Literal: "round20-kiway-reparent".
#  (3) AUI pane sizes (hunt L6): SetAuiPaneSize() forced
#      persisted pane sizes verbatim with MinSize + Fixed()
#      inside the frame -- internal AUI layout never passes
#      through the wx top-level clamp, so an era-stale size
#      could take the whole frame. Each dimension is now
#      clamped to 85% of the managed window's live client size.
#      Literal: "round20-aui-pane-clamp".
#  (4) Viewer list widths (hunt L7): the symbol and footprint
#      viewers' rescale guard divided before multiplying
#      (integer division made the library width 0 and handed
#      the whole frame to the other list) and keyed the cap off
#      the banked window width, which other frames cross-write.
#      The cap now uses the live client width when available
#      and the rescale multiplies first.
#      Literal: "round20-viewer-width-guard".
#  (5) Simulator sashes (hunt L5): SetSubWindowsSashSize()
#      applied five persisted sash positions with only a > 0
#      check, in a frame host with no shim walk and no heal
#      timer. Each is now validated against its splitter's live
#      extent (outside [10%, 90%] -> middle).
#      Literal: "round20-sim-sash-clamp".
#  (6) LaunchExternal (hunt C-3): on iOS the default-app launch
#      is refused by the sandbox, silently -- PCM Open Package
#      Directory, project-tree Open Directory / file
#      double-clicks and theme-folder buttons were dead
#      controls. A failed launch now shows a message naming the
#      path so it can be reached in Files.
#      Literal: "round20-launch-external-note".
# Apply with: patch -p1 (from the KiCad source root), after
# patches 0001-0048.
#
